      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 130,
      "outputTokens": 918,
      "costUsd": 0.008327000000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Try it on the first join, at x equals one. From the right, Q is on the line y equals two x minus one, so every secant gradient is exactly two. From the left, Q is on x squared, and the gradient is two plus h. So, one point five, one point nine, one point nine nine, heading to two. Both sides settle on two. So this function is differentiable at one, with f prime of one equal to two. The line is the tangent to x squared, so both pieces leave the join in the same direction. That's why the board doesn't jolt."
    },
