      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 124,
      "outputTokens": 831,
      "costUsd": 0.007541000000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Now the second join, where the right piece is y equals x. From the left, nothing changes. The gradients still head to two. But from the right, every secant gradient is exactly one. Two from one side, one from the other. There's no single number, so there's no derivative at x equals one. The curve is unbroken, but it isn't differentiable there. That's what a corner is: two different one-sided gradients. On the track, that's the jolt, from forty-five degrees to about sixty-three, in an instant."
    },
