      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 99,
      "outputTokens": 756,
      "costUsd": 0.0068535,
      "pronunciationText": "So at a join, check two things, in order. First, do the pieces meet? Compare the value at the join with the height the other piece heads to. If they don't meet, stop. It's not differentiable. Second, do the gradients match? Each piece here is smooth on its own side, so differentiate each one, and evaluate both at the join. Equal gradients mean differentiable. Different gradients mean a corner. Continuity on its own isn't enough."
    },
